 dict(id=33,slug='zoo-dino-tree-new-trait',title='A tree can change',hook='A newly visible feature can change a proposed grouping.',question='In a toy tree, a new feature arose once and was not lost. B and C have it; A does not. Which grouping is supported?',options=['Grouping B with C','Grouping A with B from this feature alone','Treating all three as identical'],why='The first view leaves the feature unknown; the second marks it for B and C. Under the stated single-origin and no-loss assumptions, this feature supports their grouping. Real trees require many traits and consideration of competing explanations.',recallq='In a toy tree, D and E share a new feature that arose once and was not lost; F lacks it. Which pairing is supported?',recallo=['D with E','D with F from that feature alone','No pairing can be considered'],recallwhy='Under the stipulated single-origin and no-loss assumptions, the character supports grouping D and E.',left='<text x="80" y="54" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="14" textAnchor="middle">A    B    C</text><text x="80" y="108" fill="var(--muted)" fontSize="27" textAnchor="middle">?  ?  ?</text><text x="80" y="157" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12" textAnchor="middle">Trait unknown</text>',right='<text x="260" y="54" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="14" textAnchor="middle">A    B    C</text><text x="260" y="108" fill="var(--good)" fontSize="24" textAnchor="middle">−  +  +</text><text x="260" y="157" fill="var(--fg)" fontSize="12" textAnchor="middle">Trait observed</text>',caption='Toy characters, not a real specimen analysis'),
